{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491473-place-your-bets-on-who-wins-the-jyhad-revised-v20","id":1491473,"title":"Place Your Bets on Who Wins the Jyhad [Revised/V20]","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-27T07:39:44-07:00","id":1491473,"title":"Place Your Bets on Who Wins the Jyhad [Revised/V20]","content":"The Jyhad breaks down along Clan lines. The Clans engage in both Cold and Hot War tactics to see who comes out on top. <br /> <br /> Who wins? <br /> <br /> My money's on the Tremere. Their nearest competitor are the Giovanni, but Ward vs Wraiths helps mitigate this, and Path of Spirit Manipulation creates an interesting counterbalance. Additionally, the Tremere outnumber the Giovanni so will win a battle of attrition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T09:37:27-07:00","id":1491482,"title":"","content":"I put my money on humanity winning and all the children of Caine losing the Jyhad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T09:51:49-07:00","id":1491485,"title":"","content":"The Toreador win","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T09:58:24-07:00","id":1491488,"title":"","content":"As much as I like the Brujah clan. I'd say that the Gangrel or Nosferatu have the best chance of surviving the Jyhad in all seriousness.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T10:06:01-07:00","id":1491489,"title":"","content":"Saulot. Alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T10:36:08-07:00","id":1491494,"title":"","content":"The Eldest. If it dies it just reforms in a few centuries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T11:01:37-07:00","id":1491497,"title":"","content":"Whoever win we lose. *Dramatic base drum sting*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T11:21:36-07:00","id":1491500,"title":"","content":"Saulot and Tzimisce are clearly ahead. They both are playing a long game that is still running and no one seems to be able to stop them.<br /> <br /> Augustus plan crashed with the fifth Malestrom, and the rising of the Neverborn just totally destroy the aim of the Final Night. That said, before the Maelstrom it was one of the most effective and dangerous way to win the Jyhad.<br /> <br /> Tremere is very well placed to final victory thanks to the Utah project. The Clan has almost discovered the True Name of mankind, which will give him the most powerful hermetic focus ever. Sadly the plan is quite derailed by the Worm's situation.<br /> <br /> Brujah is currently out of the Jyhad, being trapped under Carthage<br /> <br /> Toreador and Ventrue (if he is still alive) do not seem to have big plans in motions, aside for the whole Camarilla thing.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu is playing for sure, as we saw when he tried to nuke New York, and he was also the one behind the death of the Hag in Russia. Hard to say if he is &quot;winning&quot;. His Jyhad seems pretty personal and focused on the destruction of his own Clan.<br /> <br /> Ravnos bite the dust. So he is the worst place in the race. Unless the theory that Clanbook Ravnos Revised pose is true, than...who knows?<br /> <br /> Lasombra is surely as close to ascension as Tzimisce and Saulot, after becoming one with the Abyss, and he is active for sure. We see his work through the Clan Lasombra Trilogy, and through Louhi in Scandinavia. The plot to destroy the sun is surely valid, but there are a lot of if. Mystical side he surely has the advantage, since he fused himself with a Lovecraftian alien dimension of void.<br /> <br /> Malkav...who knows? The whole Malakai-Gerusalem thing pose questions about his current state.<br /> <br /> Gangrel doesn't seems to be playing the Jyhad in any significant way. Her last moves against the other antediluvians go back to Sumer, when she clashed with Toreador and stole the Typhoonic Beast from Seth.<br /> <br /> Cappadocious is out of the fight since the Maelstrom.<br /> <br /> Seth is more or less in the same situation of Brujah.<br /> <br /> Haqim also doesn't seems to be interested in the Jyhad anyomore, he left Alamut for his disdain about the whole thing.<br /> <br /> The Baali are also in pole position. Nergal has virtual control on Mexico City, and probably on the upper echelon of the Sabbat. Mahari is creating a new Well of Sacrifice in Istanbul, Ur-Shulgi has taken control of the Assamite. And as of V20 we know that the Baali are searching for the original Well of Ashur, they also took control of the Tal'Mahe'Ra through Izhim Ur-Bhaal. They play the loooong game, and they are on the rise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T12:21:16-07:00","id":1491507,"title":"","content":"Gangrel won, it's just that her victory doesn't amount to much. She fused herself with the entirety of the earth, and thereby has made every vampire who ever earthmelds her herd. That is like stealing an H-bomb just so you can force waiters to always seat you first at restaurants.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T12:26:11-07:00","id":1491508,"title":"","content":"Caine next question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27369-the-smiling-gun-knight","name":"The smiling gun-knight","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T13:59:34-07:00","id":1491517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491473-place-your-bets-on-who-wins-the-jyhad-revised-v20?p=1491482#post1491482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I put my money on humanity winning and all the children of Caine losing the Jyhad.</div> </div> </div> </div>As catastrophic as that'd be I don't think humans could ever beat vamps in a large scale conflict. Human leaders generally enjoy their priveledges over the rest of humanity and have no little interest in beating great allies, human weapons can become vampire weapons, human agents can become vampire agents, vampires can replenish their numbers at the drop of a hat, vampires can disappear for decades, centuries or millenia if it ever looks like they're losing. Unless paradox stops being a thing or someone gets lucky with invincible magic enhanced F-22s Vampires would likely win such a war even if all the mages and lupines joined hands with humanity to drive them out. The worse everything gets, the better it is for vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> Among Vampires? The Tremere and Malkavians are the best clans for this kind of struggle, but their antideluvians might be at a disadvantage and the Tremere are likely going to be everyone's first target because, y'know, the hammer that sticks out will get nailed down. Assuming he lives or Antes don't duel/get involved, my money's on Malkav. Tzmisce as-BS disease would likely win an ante-slapoff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 08-27-2022, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T16:33:32-07:00","id":1491530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491473-place-your-bets-on-who-wins-the-jyhad-revised-v20?p=1491517#post1491517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As catastrophic as that'd be I don't think humans could ever beat vamps in a large scale conflict. Human leaders generally enjoy their priveledges over the rest of humanity and have no little interest in beating great allies, human weapons can become vampire weapons, human agents can become vampire agents, vampires can replenish their numbers at the drop of a hat, vampires can disappear for decades, centuries or millenia if it ever looks like they're losing. Unless paradox stops being a thing or someone gets lucky with invincible magic enhanced F-22s Vampires would likely win such a war even if all the mages and lupines joined hands with humanity to drive them out. The worse everything gets, the better it is for vampires.<br /> <br /> <br /> Among Vampires? The Tremere and Malkavians are the best clans for this kind of struggle, but their antideluvians might be at a disadvantage and the Tremere are likely going to be everyone's first target because, y'know, the hammer that sticks out will get nailed down. Assuming he lives or Antes don't duel/get involved, my money's on Malkav. Tzmisce as-BS disease would likely win an ante-slapoff.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Technocratic Union and the Bhangadesh incident disproved this entirely. I planned a whole Mage campaign around this, called &quot;Operation Armageddon&quot;, where the Technocratic Union and the Nine Traditions declare truce to deal with the threat of Gehenna.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T16:34:51-07:00","id":1491531,"title":"","content":"No one wins.<br /> <br /> Winning is simply not in the nature of the conflict.<br /> <br /> The Jyhad is not a battle, it is a constant state of trying to get the upper hand against everyone else while avoiding becoming complete enemies because they may be your asset to have the upper hand against another.<br /> <br /> Seriously, what does it even means for the Jyhad to end? And since when does it can be so cleanly broke in clan lines? How many clan-wide alliances are there? How many vampires plot against each other within clan? What a &quot;winning&quot; would look like?<br /> <br /> Given that the Jyhad isn't supposed to be a conflict to destruction and mutual destruction is usually seen as a poor move anyway, this is all too contrived even as a question to answer. Survive the Gehenna? Valid question. Win an all-out war? Valid question. Win the Jyhad? It's like asking who'll do the checkmate in a traditional game of LoL.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T22:31:14-07:00","id":1491552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491473-place-your-bets-on-who-wins-the-jyhad-revised-v20?p=1491530#post1491530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Technocratic Union and the Bhangadesh incident disproved this entirely. I planned a whole Mage campaign around this, called &quot;Operation Armageddon&quot;, where the Technocratic Union and the Nine Traditions declare truce to deal with the threat of Gehenna.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the ancients go Godzilla one at a time, sure. If they use their 6+ intelligence ratings, I don't think so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T22:56:07-07:00","id":1491556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491473-place-your-bets-on-who-wins-the-jyhad-revised-v20?p=1491552#post1491552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the ancients go Godzilla one at a time, sure. If they use their 6+ intelligence ratings, I don't think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they use their 6+ Intelligence ratings there's no Gehenna, because it is a stupid idea.<br /> <br /> Now, if Gehenna is unavoidable, but they're allowed to use anything from 2 effective Intelligence upwards, sure.<br /> <br /> Bangladesh was the result of an ancient acting with the smarts of a potato.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-27T23:44:23-07:00","id":1491558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491473-place-your-bets-on-who-wins-the-jyhad-revised-v20?p=1491552#post1491552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the ancients go Godzilla one at a time, sure. If they use their 6+ intelligence ratings, I don't think so.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technocrat and Traditions Archmasters are just as smart, and Thaumaturgy can't match Archspheres. Nah, they better hope Caine comes back. Vampires are not overlords, they're parasites who need to hide from an enraged humanity.<br /> <br /> Banglafesh was the results of a ancient acting <i>in character</i> and <i>in-lore</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6358-robert-armsley","name":"Robert Armsley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6358_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T04:58:46-07:00","id":1491582,"title":"","content":"I'm not arguing Mages vs Vampires. Just pointing out that it was noted that Ravnos in Bangladesh was locked into Wassail. He was a mindless, ravening godlike beast, but he absolutely wasn't using any sort of intelligence or tactics. Had he retained his intellect that scenario would have been vastly different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T06:47:08-07:00","id":1491588,"title":"","content":"Saulot will become the Demon Emperor. Tzimisce just *is*. Gangrel doesn't GAF. Auggie is slain by Harbingers and traitors. Tremere is trapped in the body of a Methuselah. Lasombra just *is*... the Abyss. <br /> <br /> Troile dreams of happy-fun-sacrificial-torture times with Moloch. Malkav just is... Madness itself. Ventrue is possibly dead, but no one cares either way. Toreador has other things to attend to (staring at the infinite eldritch beauty of Lasombra or Malkav, perhaps). <br /> <br /> Nosferatu slays all his childer and becomes beautiful again. Set is dead and loathing it. Ravnos is probably dead, or a dream, but he's of no concern to anyone but the fae anymore.<br /> <br /> Caine will return and slaughter all of the ones who aren't alien things existing in their own twisted little utopias. Saulot will probably fall last.<br /> <br /> Then Lilith slays Caine and turns the Wheel of Ages to the Seventh Age, before flying back up to Heaven on Lucifer's wings to claim Yahweh's empty throne. When she's finished her project of progressing things to the point of beginning again, we'll be back at the First Age again... Where it'll happen all over again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":". 08-30-2022, 10:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T07:41:26-07:00","id":1491590,"title":"","content":"The one guy who rises up and starts wrecking shit only to get blasted just so happens to be the master of Chimestry. Will the rest of Gehenna be like that? Press X to doubt.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Semi-sensible Reasons for Gehenna:<br /> Antes spot a window to true immortality/1st gen/godhood/something really good and rush to be the one to get it.<br /> \u200bThe world's gonna end anyway so the Antes just roll with it.<br /> Actually most of the Antes have really strong grievances but they weren't getting anywhere so they agreed to slumber till 202X where they could do more damage.<br /> Saulot/Tzmisce/Lasombra/Ventrue/Capadocious/whatever has a pretty good plan for world domination and nobody wants to be left behind.<br /> Human progress and and the general movement towards equality is going to make it very hard for vampires to continue unliving so the ancients agree to wake up and overturn the status quo in favour of something that works better for vampires (Fascism).<br /> <br /> Honestly, there's not many. I too think the Antes would probably do -business as usual- if they woke up. &quot;Gehenna&quot; would most likely be a lie spread among elders who fear their power usurped by sleeping ancients who might just wake up and take over or who wish to justify their persecution/Diablerie of sleeping ancients. Fear is an excelent tool for having people acting against their best interests.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T08:09:44-07:00","id":1491596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Armsley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491473-place-your-bets-on-who-wins-the-jyhad-revised-v20?p=1491558#post1491558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technocrat and Traditions Archmasters are just as smart, and Thaumaturgy can't match Archspheres. Nah, they better hope Caine comes back. Vampires are not overlords, they're parasites who need to hide from an enraged humanity.<br /> <br /> Banglafesh was the results of a ancient acting <i>in character</i> and <i>in-lore</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Archmasters don't exist in Vampire games unless the ST says so. The books aren't written with the assumption that other splats exist as they do in their own lines, and your assertions take a lot of things for granted just to reinforce your opinion. It is arguable if Archspheres exist even within Mage, given that a <b>lot</b> of STs don't like and don't use such rules, and the books themselves make very little use of them outside the book they were presented.<br /> <br /> There's no description of [Ravnos] in the Bangladesh debacle, much less reason to conclude it is a parameter for how things would be with anyone else. Other books had ancients behaving in very different ways and with very different abilities.<br /> <br /> Making a game about Mages fighting down the antes to prevent Gehenna may be a lot of fun. Coming to a Vampire thread to shit on the line saying Mages would win the Jyhad and the Gehenna because they're obviously superior in your interpretation is just BS.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T23:38:49-07:00","id":1491713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491473-place-your-bets-on-who-wins-the-jyhad-revised-v20?p=1491500#post1491500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Saulot and Tzimisce are clearly ahead. They both are playing a long game that is still running and no one seems to be able to stop them.<br /> <br /> Augustus plan crashed with the fifth Malestrom, and the rising of the Neverborn just totally destroy the aim of the Final Night. That said, before the Maelstrom it was one of the most effective and dangerous way to win the Jyhad.<br /> <br /> Tremere is very well placed to final victory thanks to the Utah project. The Clan has almost discovered the True Name of mankind, which will give him the most powerful hermetic focus ever. Sadly the plan is quite derailed by the Worm's situation.<br /> <br /> Brujah is currently out of the Jyhad, being trapped under Carthage<br /> <br /> Toreador and Ventrue (if he is still alive) do not seem to have big plans in motions, aside for the whole Camarilla thing.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu is playing for sure, as we saw when he tried to nuke New York, and he was also the one behind the death of the Hag in Russia. Hard to say if he is &quot;winning&quot;. His Jyhad seems pretty personal and focused on the destruction of his own Clan.<br /> <br /> Ravnos bite the dust. So he is the worst place in the race. Unless the theory that Clanbook Ravnos Revised pose is true, than...who knows?<br /> <br /> Lasombra is surely as close to ascension as Tzimisce and Saulot, after becoming one with the Abyss, and he is active for sure. We see his work through the Clan Lasombra Trilogy, and through Louhi in Scandinavia. The plot to destroy the sun is surely valid, but there are a lot of if. Mystical side he surely has the advantage, since he fused himself with a Lovecraftian alien dimension of void.<br /> <br /> Malkav...who knows? The whole Malakai-Gerusalem thing pose questions about his current state.<br /> <br /> Gangrel doesn't seems to be playing the Jyhad in any significant way. Her last moves against the other antediluvians go back to Sumer, when she clashed with Toreador and stole the Typhoonic Beast from Seth.<br /> <br /> Cappadocious is out of the fight since the Maelstrom.<br /> <br /> Seth is more or less in the same situation of Brujah.<br /> <br /> Haqim also doesn't seems to be interested in the Jyhad anyomore, he left Alamut for his disdain about the whole thing.<br /> <br /> The Baali are also in pole position. Nergal has virtual control on Mexico City, and probably on the upper echelon of the Sabbat. Mahari is creating a new Well of Sacrifice in Istanbul, Ur-Shulgi has taken control of the Assamite. And as of V20 we know that the Baali are searching for the original Well of Ashur, they also took control of the Tal'Mahe'Ra through Izhim Ur-Bhaal. They play the loooong game, and they are on the rise.</div> </div> </div> </div>in retrospect seens obvious, but i never though the baali took control of the assamite. probably true D:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24832-blailton","name":"blailton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24832_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"389"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T03:45:10-07:00","id":1491733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The smiling gun-knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491473-place-your-bets-on-who-wins-the-jyhad-revised-v20?p=1491508#post1491508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Caine next question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assuming the Book of Nod isn't just propaganda, this is the answer. It ends with Caine returning to pass judgement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T04:08:11-07:00","id":1491735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491473-place-your-bets-on-who-wins-the-jyhad-revised-v20?p=1491733#post1491733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assuming the Book of Nod isn't just propaganda, this is the answer. It ends with Caine returning to pass judgement.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it's propaganda. Toreador wins","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T06:08:26-07:00","id":1491751,"title":"","content":"Lilith wins by telling Caine to finally clean up his mess and then go to his room without dinner, under threat of <i>la chancla</i><br /> <br /> Set throws a tantrum, declares himself winner anyways, and crafts himself a Best Dad Of The Aeon trophy. Tremere does the same and tells everyone he did it first.<br /> <br /> Saulot realizes he actually has no end-game plan, creates 42 new bloodlines and hopes he will figure it out during the next round.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-29T19:14:37-07:00","id":1491854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491473-place-your-bets-on-who-wins-the-jyhad-revised-v20?p=1491751#post1491751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lilith wins by telling Caine to finally clean up his mess and then go to his room without dinner, under threat of <i>la chancla</i><br /> <br /> Set throws a tantrum, declares himself winner anyways, and crafts himself a Best Dad Of The Aeon trophy. Tremere does the same and tells everyone he did it first.<br /> <br /> Saulot realizes he actually has no end-game plan, creates 42 new bloodlines and hopes he will figure it out during the next round.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In the background, Arikel is taking selfies and uploading them to Instagram","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T04:09:01-07:00","id":1491993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491473-place-your-bets-on-who-wins-the-jyhad-revised-v20?p=1491531#post1491531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No one wins.<br /> <br /> Winning is simply not in the nature of the conflict.<br /> <br /> The Jyhad is not a battle, it is a constant state of trying to get the upper hand against everyone else while avoiding becoming complete enemies because they may be your asset to have the upper hand against another.<br /> <br /> Seriously, what does it even means for the Jyhad to end? And since when does it can be so cleanly broke in clan lines? How many clan-wide alliances are there? How many vampires plot against each other within clan? What a &amp;quot;winning&amp;quot; would look like?<br /> <br /> Given that the Jyhad isn't supposed to be a conflict to destruction and mutual destruction is usually seen as a poor move anyway, this is all too contrived even as a question to answer. Survive the Gehenna? Valid question. Win an all-out war? Valid question. Win the Jyhad? It's like asking who'll do the checkmate in a traditional game of LoL.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;It is the mark of an educated mind to be able to entertain a thought without accepting it.&quot;<br /> - Aristotle","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27252-hades","name":"Hades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"110"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T11:55:41-07:00","id":1492022,"title":"","content":"The next best question is which of the antidulivans decided that the Jyhad was a waste of time and decided not to play anymore?<br /> <br /> In that case we have the Gangrel who withdrew earlier then some and decided to become melded with the Earth and doesn't seem to show much interest in her clan actions at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T15:04:55-07:00","id":1492038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1491473-place-your-bets-on-who-wins-the-jyhad-revised-v20?p=1492022#post1492022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The next best question is which of the antidulivans decided that the Jyhad was a waste of time and decided not to play anymore?<br /> <br /> In that case we have the Gangrel who withdrew earlier then some and decided to become melded with the Earth and doesn't seem to show much interest in her clan actions at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually think a number of them left the game one way or another, already.<br /> <br /> What follows is my personal take for now. I may change my mind.<br /> <br /> <b>Brujah/Troile:</b> buried in Carthage, dead or isolated from the time-stream for too much time. The clan is effectively left to its own devices;<br /> <br /> <b>Ventrue/Siddartha:</b> faked its own death and retired from the Jyhad after noticing that continued development of <b>Dominate</b> and their role in the eternal conflict would mean Ego Death. Now struggles constantly to <i>avoid</i> such fate and keep its grasp on personal identity, maybe also interfering to disrupt mental powers in general, I'm not sure;<br /> <br /> <b>Toreador/Arikel:</b> retired to seek ways to recover its humanity in some sense. Currently lives as most Neonates, keeping a human facade with a human job and human activities, and particularly enjoy leading people through letters, and now the internet, in order to nullify its own preternatural advantages, both as a means to study people and for the pleasure of the challenge;<br /> <br /> <b>Malkav:</b> lost in the depths of the Madness Network, which is the living-but-non-sentient manifestation of <b>Dementation</b>. Effectively retired despite still extremely influential in the Jyhad;<br /> <br /> <b>Gangrel/Ennoia:</b> playing a dangerous game, actually. I always found it deeply weird that a clan with such an uninvolved take to Embrace had such a uniform outlook. I think it isn't actually as disinterested as it always pretended to be, and whispers in the ears of its childer with the goal of causing this culture to take hold for its own end goals. But by doing so, risks being truly engulfed by its melding with Earth just as so many think it did. I'm undecided if it avoided such fate or not;<br /> <br /> <b>Nosferatu/Absimiliard:</b> technically in the Jyhad, but too self-loathing and self-centered to actually be of any consequence. In a sense, the opposite of Malkav, making some effort to participate, but ultimately being inconsequential even to most of its childer;<br /> <br /> <b>Tremere:</b> at large in Goratrix's body, maybe he even kept the 3rd gen powers, who knows. Still game, but recovering from a severe setback after the loss to Saulot;<br /> <br /> <b>Lasombra:</b> deceased. Was a goner even before Gratiano's invasion of the castle, the 4th gen just found out the faint vestiges of a body dissolving into the Abyss and decided that gloating about killing the Ante was better than telling the clan they had been afraid for year from an empty room;<br /> <br /> <b>Tzimisce/Eldest:</b> still game, leaving behind creations from pieces of its body that acquired their own existence. Its true body may be any or none of them, but while originally it sought out Apotheosis Through Metamorphosis, its participation in the Jyhad isn't really a part of this, but just a side diversion that amuses it;<br /> <br /> <b>Cappadocius:</b> not a vampire anymore, dead but doing fine, thank you. As the Jyhad never interested it, current plans and goals reside mainly outside the material plane;<br /> <br /> <b>Set/Suthek:</b> trying to play 5-D chess with everyone, and I mean everyone, even for an Ante it tried to swallow something bigger than its mouth. Simply being &quot;alive&quot; at this point is proof of its cunning, but as its too many allies and foes get and lose land all the time it is hard to say where it stands at any given time. It does a very good job at pretending to be in charge, but it doesn't completely control not even its own cults all the time. If the Jyhad ever ends, it will lose any will to live;<br /> <br /> <b>Haqim:</b> comes and goes from the Jyhad. It despises this game, want nothing to do with it and wisely suggest others to leave, but at the same time it's just too good a player, always seeing opportunities to further its lofty goals through the Jyhad. Do as I say, not as I do, it may achieve to stay away for decades at a time to then come back as an addict;<br /> <br /> <b>Ravnos/Zapathasura:</b> wassail. Simply lost to its own Beast. The thing killed in Bangladesh was barely more than an animal, powerful as it was;<br /> <br /> <b>Augustus Giovanni:</b> so paranoid with Cappadocius' Wraith that it never believed itself to have truly achieved complete Diablerie, but it was actually exactly that. It either died at the hands of the Hecata or pays lip service to the Jyhad while actually delegating decisions to wander the Umbra in search of Cappadocius;<br /> <br /> <b>Salubri/Saulot:</b> still playing the Jyhad, sometimes against itself as it changes plans and has to work towards undoing what it did before. The key difference between it and Set is that Set <i><b>pretends</b></i> to have everything under control, Saulot <i><b>tries</b></i> to have everything under control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-31T17:04:32-07:00","id":1492047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Lasombra:</b> deceased. Was a goner even before Gratiano's invasion of the castle, the 4th gen just found out the faint vestiges of a body dissolving into the Abyss and decided that gloating about killing the Ante was better than telling the clan they had been afraid for year from an empty room; </div> </div> </div>Isn't that usually the kind of thing that would make you worry that your sire had faked their own death somehow?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted Whose Name is Carved in Leaves of Jade<br /> Senator of the Greater Chamber<br /> Champion of the Silver Pact<br /> Chosen of the Little Gods<br /> Agent of Fate","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/988-mizu","name":"Mizu","a